27::
0:
IO & Communication
1000:
Bus name invalid\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Driver %s: has an invalid bus name\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change the busname for the driver
1001:
Duplicated address\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Same address for unit %s and %s\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1.Check the address\n
2.Check the bus
1002:
Invalid driver\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Unit %s: has an unspecified driver\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1.Check the drivers against the one\n
  specified for the unit
1003:
Invalid unit\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The unit specified for the signal %s\n
  is not specified in the unit section\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1.Change the name of the unit\n
2.Add a new unit to the unit list
1004:
Invalid signal length\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The length of the digital\n
  signal %s must be 1\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1.Change the length to 1 or remove\n
  the statement.
1005:
Filter time invalid\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal %s: The passive filter time\n
  should be 0 or %d - %d ms\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1.Change the filter time
1006:
Filter time invalid\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal %s: The active filter time\n
  should be 0 or %d - %d ms\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1.Change the filter time
1007:
Logic. value out of range\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal %s: Logical Max is less or\n
  equal to Logical Min\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1.Correct the values to be max greater\n
  than min
1008:
Phys. value out of range\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal %s: Physical Max is less or\n
  equal to Physical Min\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1.Correct the values to be max greater\n
  than min
1009:
Type invalid\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal %s: the type of signal\n
  is invalid\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1.Change the type
1010:
Signal out of range\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal %s: the physical signal\n
  number + length -1 is > %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1.Change the physical signal number\n
2.Change the length
1011:
Driver not supported\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The driver %s is not supported\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change the name of the driver
1012:
Memory overflow\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Board %s: Too many boards\n
  for specified driver type\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change number of boards for the\n
   driver at driver configuration.
1013:
Wrong type of board\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Wrong type of board connected\n
  to address %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check the board type at given address
1014:
Board missing\n
Description\Reason:\n
- No board connected at given\n
  address %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Connect a board to the slot\n
2. Change the board address
1015:
Digital Input overflow\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Number of digital input channels\n
  for board %s is greater\n
  than %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reduce the number digital inputs
1016:
Digital Output overflow\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Number of digital output channels\n
  for board %s is greater\n
  than %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reduce the number of digital outputs
1017:
No activate signal\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Missing activate signal for cross\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. One activate signal must be given
1018:
Activate signal overflow\n
Description\Reason:\n
-Number of activate signals for\n
 cross too high\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Only one activate signal must\n
   be given
1019:
Missing signal definition\n
Description\Reason:\n
-The signal: %s, at cross is\n
 not defined\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Define the signal name\n
   in signal section
1020:
No result signal\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Missing result signal\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. At least one result signal must\n
   be given
1021:
Duplicate cross signals\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The signal: %s, appears both as FROM\n
  and as TO.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. The same signal can not be given for\n
   both FROM and TO
1022:
Physical max too high\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal: %s\n
- The physical max value > %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change value in configuration
1023:
Physical min too low\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal: %s\n
- The physical min value < %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change value in configuration
1024:
Physical value too high\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal: %s\n
- Current value = %d > Maxvalue = %d\n
- Value set to Maxvalue\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change physical max value in\n
   configuration
1025:
Physical value too low\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal: %s\n
- Current value = %d < Minvalue = %d\n
- Value set to Minvalue\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change physical min value in\n
   configuration
1026:
Logical value too high\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal: %s\n
- Current value = %d > Maxvalue = %d\n
- Value set to Maxvalue\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change logical max value in\n
   configuration
1027:
Logical value too low\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal: %s\n
- Current value = %d < Minvalue = %d\n
- Value set to Minvalue\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change logical min value in\n
   configuration
1028:
Config. out of range\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The RIO starting quarter and rack\n
  size is out of range for\n
  board %s\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. For starting quarter 0 rack size\n
   must be less than 4
1029:
Config. out of range\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The RIO starting quarter and rack\n
  size is out of range for\n
  board %s\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. For starting quarter 1 rack size\n
   must be less than 3
1030:
Config. out of range\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The RIO starting quarter and rack\n
  size is out of range for\n
  board %s\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. For starting quarter 2 rack size\n
   must be less than 2
1031:
Config. out of range\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The RIO starting quarter and rack\n
  size is out of range for\n
  board %s\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. For starting quarter 3 rack size\n
   must be 0
1032:
Communication fail\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The RIO board has lost communication\n
  with the PLC at board\n
  address %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check the communication cable to PLC\n
2. Check of if the PLC is switched off
1033:
Dig. input out of range\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The number of digital inputs is\n
  out of range at board address %d\n
  max inputs are %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change the configuration for\n
   the board
1034:
Dig. output out of range\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The number of digital outputs is\n
  out of range at board address %d\n
  max outputs are %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change the configuration for\n
   the board
1035:
Start quart. out of range\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The starting quarter is\n
  out of range for board %s\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. The starting quarter must be within\n
   the values 0 to 3. change the config\n
   file.
1036:
Name out of range\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The number of characters in\n
- name %s\n
- is greater than %d characters or\n
- the name is missing.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Give a new name that fits within\n
   the limits.
1037:
IO Cross connection fault\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The signal %s appears on both\n
  FROM and TO in the same chain\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Correct the configuration for the\n
cross connections where the signal above\n
is connected.
1038:
IO Cross depth to high\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The Cross connection in the same chain\n
- is too deep.\n
- First signal name: %s\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Make the Cross connection less deep.
1039:
Max instance out of range\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The max number of instances for\n
- driver %s is out of range.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Make sure that the number of\n
   instances is greater than 0,\n
   and not more than number of IO slots.
1040:
RIO link addr out of rang\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The RIO link address for board\n
- %s is out of range.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Make sure that the RIO link address\n
   is greater than 0, and less than 64.
1041:
Analog output overflow\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Number of analog output for\n
- board, %s is greater than %d.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reduce the number of analog outputs.
1042:
Analog inputs overflow\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Number of analog inputs for\n
- board, %s is greater than %d.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reduce the number of analog inputs.
1043:
Signal type error\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The type specified for signal %s\n
 can't be connected to specified board\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change to another type.\n
2. Change to another board.
1044:
Physical signal overflow\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The range of phsig, or length, or\n
  phsig and length for signal %s is\n
  greater than %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change the physical signal number\n
2. Change the length.
1045:
Filter specification err.\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal %s : No filter time can be\n
  specified for this type of signal.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Set filter time to 0 or remove the\n
   statement.
1046:
Scaling error\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal %s: No scaling can be done.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Remove the scaling statements.
1049:
Parameter Invert error\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal %s: This type of signal\n
 can't be inverted.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Only digital signals can be inverted.
1050:
Cross signal not digital.\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal %s: Is not a digital signal\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Only digital signals can be cross.\n
   connected.
1051:
Link address not octal.\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal %s: The RIO address is not in\n
  octal form\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reenter a new address in octal form.
1052:
Cross table full.\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The sum of different FROM signals\n
  added with total sum of TO signals\n
  must not exceed %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reduce the number of signals.\n
2. Increase the number of crosscon.\n
   allowed.
1053:
Connection to board down\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Can't access the board due to\n
  communication is down\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check the communication cable to\n
   the board\n
2. Check if the board is switched off
1054:
Wrong signal type\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal %s:\n
  The type of signal is wrong\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change the type
1055:
Invalid signal name\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Symbol %s: is not defined\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Change the symbol name above
1056:
Power fail restore full\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Symbol %s: could not be setup for\n
  power failure restore.\n
  The table for power fail is full.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Increase the table size in\n
   startup file.\n
2. Remove some other signal from restore\n
   list.
1057:
DSQC319 Board missing\n
Description\Reason:\n
- No board of type DSQC319\n
  connected at address %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Connect a board to the slot\n
2. Change the board address
1058:
No contact with Can node\n
Description\Reason:\n
- No contact with Can node\n
  connected at node address %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check the node addresses on all\n
   can modules connected to the can bus\n
2. Change the node address
1059:
Error config. Can node\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Error when configuring Can node\n
  connected at node address %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Correct the configuration for the\n
   Can node at given address.
1060:
DSQC319 Internal error\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The DSQC319 board\n
  connected at address %d\n
  have an internal error\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check if the CAN bus works correcltly\n
2. Check if DSQC319 works correctly
1061:
Can bus error\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Abnormal occurrenses of error\n
  on the Can bus connected to DSQC319\n
  at address %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check the communication cable to\n
   the Can bus
1062:
D319 receive buffer full\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Receive buffer is full on board\n
  connected at address %d.\n
  Messages may be lost\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reduce the number of nodes on the\n
   Can bus.
1063:
Can message lost\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Can messages is lost on board\n
  connected at address %d.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reduce the number of nodes on the\n
   Can bus.
1064:
IOC generated fault\n
Description\Reason:\n
- IOC signals fault to the\n
  dsqc260 board at address %d.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check the IOC.
1065:
DSQC260 generated fault\n
Description\Reason:\n
- DSQC260 board at address %d\n
  signals fault.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check the dsqc260 board.
1066:
InterBus-S inactive\n
Description\Reason:\n
- InterBus-S connected to\n
  dsqc260 board at address %d\n
  inactive.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check the InterBus-S nodes.
1067:
InterBus-S unconnected\n
Description\Reason:\n
- InterBus-S attached to\n
  dsqc260 board at address %d\n
  unconnected or IBS master\n
  in reset mode.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check the InterBus-S nodes.\n
2. Check the InterBus-S master.
1068:
IOC OK\n
Description\Reason:\n
- IOC previously faulty, now OK.\n
  Fault message was sent to\n
  dsqc260 board at address %d.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Do nothing.
1069:
DSQC260 OK\n
Description\Reason:\n
- DSQC260 board at address %d\n
  previously faulty, now OK.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Do nothing.
1070:
InterBus-S active\n
Description\Reason:\n
- InterBus-S connected to\n
  dsqc260 board at address %d\n
  previously inactive, now OK.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Do nothing.
1071:
InterBus-S connected\n
Description\Reason:\n
- InterBus-S attached to\n
  dsqc260 board at address %d\n
  previously unconnected or IBS master\n
  in reset mode, now OK.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Do nothing.
1072:
No save set on signal\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal %s\n
  has not Set the Store attribute to YES\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Set the Store attribute.
1073:
Cont establ with Can node\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Contact established with Can node\n
  connected at node address %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Do nothing.
1074:
Config. out of range\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The IBS starting quarter and rack\n
  size is out of range for\n
  board %s\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. For starting quarter 1 rack size\n
   must be less than 5
1075:
Access error from IO\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Cannot Read or Write from/to IO\n
  board due to communication down\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check com.fail report for reason
1076:
Comm error from rtp1\n
Description\Reason:\n
- No response from the\n
  serial line\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check the device or connection
1077:
Comm error from rtp1\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Not possible to deliver\n
  the received message\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check the communication flow
1078:
Comm error from rtp1\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The response from the device\n
  has a non valid frame sequence\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check for noise on the serial\n
   line
1079:
Pulsing group output\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Pulsing group output not allowed.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. ---
1080:
Driver table full.\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The number of drivers\n
  must not exceed %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reduce the number of drivers.\n
2. Increase the number of drivers\n
   allowed.
1081:
Physical table full.\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The number of physical signals\n
  must not exceed %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reduce the number of physical\n
   signals.\n
2. Increase the number of phs allowed.
1082:
Signal table full.\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The number of user defined signals\n
  must not exceed %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reduce the number of signals.\n
2. Increase the number of signals\n
   allowed.
1083:
Symbol table full.\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The number of symbols\n
  must not exceed %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reduce the number of symbols.\n
2. Increase the number of symbols\n
   allowed.
1084:
Triggr table full.\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The number of Subcribed signals\n
  must not exceed %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reduce the number of Subcribed\n
   signals.\n
2. Increase the number of Subcribtions\n
   allowed.
1085:
Unit table full.\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The number of boards\n
  must not exceed %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Reduce the number of dfined boards.\n
2. Increase the number of boards\n
   allowed.
1086:
Com. OK with RIO\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Contact established with RIO node\n
  connected at node address %d\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Do nothing.
1094:
Too many cross-actors def\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The cross-connection has too\n
  many "From" signals : %s\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check the cross configuration.
1095:
Too long cross-actor str\n
Description\Reason:\n
- The "From" part in the cross-string\n
  is too long : %s\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Check the cross configuration.
1096:
PLC in programming mode\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Can't access the board due to\n
  the PLC in programming mode\n
  or the it is configured\n
  incorrectly.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. PLC in programming mode\n
2. Check PLC configuration
1097:
Parameter store error\n
Description\Reason:\n
- Signal %s: This type of signal\n
 can't have store option.\n
\t\n
Check list:\n
1. Only digital signals can have store.
